    "title": "Tampa police investigate bomb threat near downtown bank - NewsBreak",
    "text": "TAMPA, Florida — The Tampa Police Department is investigating a bomb threat reported in the 200 block of N. Franklin St. Officers responded around 2:20 p.m. after an anonymous caller claimed an explosive device was outside the 1st Horizon Bank. Members of the Tampa Police Bomb Unit assisted in the investigation, and officers conducted interviews in the area. Currently, there is no evidence suggesting an active threat to public safety, according to the Tampa Police Department. \"Making threats of explosives or any other dangerous device is a serious criminal offense,\" said Chief Lee Bercaw. \"These types of calls are not only illegal, but also create disruption, waste valuable public resources, and cause unnecessary concern for our community. Those found responsible for making such threats will be prosecuted to the full extent of the law.\" The investigation remains active, and updates will be provided as they become available, stated the department.",
